# armour/man/leather: studded leather on the man (P2c slice, SLICE-ARMOUR; STYLE_P2 25.2-25.3): a boiled-leather
# cuirass over the tunic (light: the civilian silhouette kept), matte and warm, a step-3 top edge, ONE step-1 stitch line
# (the centre seam facing down and up), a brass-buckled belt, one step-4 shine on the lit shoulder and no glint. The studs
# are the `when studs` region: ONE course of metal-2 pixels, every other pixel on the lit planes of the row over the stitch
# line (i3: the 3 px scatter read as camo speckle at 1x). Broad matte planes (lit step 3, turn step 2, shade step 1), no
# alternating rows. The tunic's sleeves show (the
# resolver's leather region: a bracer on the forearm with the stitch tile). The tunic (cloth1) shows at the collar, the throat's V and the
# man's shoulder caps; the jerkin is closed down the flanks (i3). Keys: rest idle run runl drawn swing lie in
# D U R L. Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
use person
body man
role armour leather
layer torso
anchor neck
keys torso
z 2

